 "method": "    python training/benchmark_cf.py --data-dir ml-32m --user-sample 5 Rule written before running: - Same MovieLens positives (4+ stars), same per-user time split, same users for every model. - Models: popularity, the current SVD embeddings (64 dims), SVD 128 dims, item-kNN (cosine with   shrinkage), implicit ALS, EASE (closed-form linear), and top-100-neighbor versions of item-kNN and   EASE that are small enough to ship. - Hyperparameters are chosen on 3,000 validation users. Results are reported on 3,000 different   test users, once. - Onboarding is scored with 3 RANDOM likes from each viewer's history (the honest case). The   last-3 version used before is also reported, because recent likes sit closest to what comes next. - A model replaces the current SVD in the app only if, on random-3 seeds, it beats it on Hit@1 and   NDCG@10 with paired-bootstrap 95% intervals above zero, and its model file is under 25 MB. Writes data/cf_benchmark.json. ",
